# Finding 016

## Title

Agility Metrics Show Positive Relationship with NFL Career Usage

---

## Context

Following the route-specific skill framework established in Milestone 03,
SLANT_ROUTE_LEFT was selected as the primary drill for evaluating agility.

The objective was to determine whether tracking-derived agility metrics
show meaningful relationships with NFL career outcomes.

---

## Drill

```text
SLANT_ROUTE_LEFT
```

Sample:

```text
107 route attempts
```

---

## Metrics Evaluated

Tracking Metrics:

- direction_change_mean
- agility_index_mean

Definitions:

```text
direction_change_mean

Average cumulative directional change during route execution.
```

```text
agility_index_mean

direction_change / route_duration
```

Designed to capture directional change relative to route execution time.

NFL Outcomes:

- career_games_started
- career_offensive_snaps

---

## Results

### Agility Index

```text
agility_index_mean ↔ career_games_started

r = 0.274
```

```text
agility_index_mean ↔ career_offensive_snaps

r = 0.328
```

